ModelTrace numerical fingerprint scorer and reference bank
Source: https://github.com/xqy2006/ModelTrace
Revision: 55a2e4a

The Go scoring implementation adapts fingerprint.py and static/fingerprint-core.js.
data/unified_bank.json preserves the upstream model counts, robust features and
calibration, with unused presentation/collection metadata removed. Small samples
in testdata/reference.json are from data/gpt_reference.jsonl and
data/claude_reference.jsonl; each fixture retains its upstream row ID and source.
The reference bank is a finite candidate set. Its softmax probability is relative
to those candidates and does not authenticate a model or measure intelligence.
Local JSON and pattern validation is intentionally stricter than upstream parsing.

